# Cross-origin isolation for the wasm edit-host (Phase 5). The Web Worker drives its
# run loop off a SharedArrayBuffer (slice 5d), which the browser only exposes when the
# document is cross-origin isolated. These three headers make `crossOriginIsolated`
# true; without them the page falls back to the slower postMessage transport and timers
# (vim.defer_fn / nx.timer) never fire.
#
# This is the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format — drop `web/` (this dir) and
# the built `dist/` alongside it as the publish root. For nginx / Apache / other hosts,
# set the same three headers on every response (see README → "Serving in production").
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
